UniSEM first-stage EMNeuron model and source-domain RF

This distribution contains a modified derivative of the Segment Anything
ViT-L model by Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates. SAM is licensed under
Apache License 2.0. The original copyright and license notices remain applicable.
https://github.com/facebookresearch/segment-anything

Modifications: first-stage EMNeuron training, prompt-free dense decoding,
HQ-inspired cross-layer refinement, and a reduced inference export that omits
unused interactive heads and optimizer/training metadata. The accompanying
random forest was fitted for the ordered 55-feature source-domain pipeline.

EMNeuron dataset: https://huggingface.co/datasets/yanchaoz/EMNeuron
The official dataset card declares MIT at revision
62df92b933550cc2a5d3849fe8543191c356f2d4. No training images are redistributed.

The implementation builds on micro-SAM, torch-em, ELF, the SAM-HQ refinement
idea, and LoRA. These projects retain their own source-code licenses and
publication attribution. Official HQ-SAM refinement weights are not included.

The upstream statements above describe the sources reviewed for this release;
they do not relicense external datasets or the separate target-model assets.
